{"nodes": [{"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_hierarchy_of_blocks", "label": "Hierarchy of Overlapping Blocks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Precompute aggregates over a hierarchy of blocks instead of over every prefix: a range decomposes into Theta(log n) precomputed pieces and a point update touches only the Theta(log n) blocks containing it. That single idea produces Fenwick, segment tree, and sqrt decomposition \u2014 they differ only in which hierarchy they use."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_tree", "label": "Fenwick Tree (Binary Indexed Tree)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Fenwick tree", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "tree[i] holds the aggregate of the i & (-i) elements ending at i \u2014 each index owns a range the length of its lowest set bit. One array of size n, no pointers, no recursion. Measured 3.9 ms vs ~5,623 ms naive rescan (~1,400x) for 100k interleaved updates and queries over n=10^6, and the ratio grows linearly with n."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_segment_tree", "label": "Segment Tree", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Segment tree", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stores a genuine aggregate per range node and answers by COMBINING Theta(log n) disjoint nodes rather than subtracting two prefixes \u2014 so no inverse is required and any associative operation works. Costs 2n memory and a larger constant; earns it only for non-invertible ops or lazy range updates."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_lazy_propagation", "label": "Lazy Propagation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Lazy propagation", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Maintains a second invariant \u2014 a node's aggregate is correct assuming all pending ancestor updates have been applied \u2014 so every access path must push down first and pull up after. Funnel all node access through push_down/pull_up helpers so skipping is structurally impossible, then property-test with a brute-force checker."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_sparse_table", "label": "Sparse Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "The Invariant", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "st[k][i] covers 2^k elements from i; a query uses two OVERLAPPING blocks, which is safe only because the operation is idempotent (min, max, gcd). Theta(1) queries at Theta(n log n) space and no updates at all."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_sqrt_decomposition", "label": "Sqrt Decomposition", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Sqrt decomposition", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Theta(sqrt n) \u2014 ~1,000 ops at n=10^6 vs a segment tree's ~20 \u2014 but trivially adaptable to weird aggregates (range mode, distinct count) where no logarithmic structure is obvious. Mo's algorithm builds on it for offline query batching."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_1_indexing", "label": "Fenwick 1-Indexing Encapsulation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The structure depends on the lowest set bit and 0 has none, so i -= i & (-i) at i=0 is an infinite loop. Keep the 1-indexing strictly inside the type and expose a 0-indexed half-open API so the conversion happens in exactly one place."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_non_commutative_accumulators", "label": "Separate Left/Right Accumulators for Non-Commutative Ops", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The iterative bottom-up query walks in from both ends; one accumulator combines pieces out of order. Harmless for + and min, silently wrong for matrix products or string concatenation \u2014 so the bug appears only when the structure is reused, long after it was trusted."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_over_difference_array", "label": "Fenwick over a Difference Array", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Choosing: the decision table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Range update with point query in two calls \u2014 add(l,+v), add(r+1,-v), and a point query becomes a prefix sum. The cheapest trick in the topic; no lazy propagation needed."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_does_the_data_change", "label": "Decision Rule: Does the Data Change?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model / Pitfalls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The entire hierarchy exists to make UPDATES cheap; with no updates you pay for a capability you don't use, and pay in the query path. Static data: prefix sums are three lines, Theta(1), and FASTER than a tree (2 reads vs ~20 scattered). Ask this first, not last."}], "edges": [{"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_over_difference_array", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_difference_array", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Choosing: the decision table", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_bloom_filter", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_sqrt_decomposition", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "AMBIGUOUS", "confidence_score": 0.2, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Creative lens 'Approximate it' names sketches as the approximate counterpart of a range structure", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_randomized_algorithms_learning_seed_reproducibility", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_lazy_propagation", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Both prescribe proptest-driven invariant checking against a brute-force oracle", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_tree", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_hierarchy_of_blocks", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_segment_tree", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_hierarchy_of_blocks", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_sqrt_decomposition", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_hierarchy_of_blocks", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_lazy_propagation", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_segment_tree", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Lazy propagation", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_segment_tree", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_tree", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfall: Building a Fenwick tree for min or max", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_1_indexing", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_tree", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_non_commutative_accumulators", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_segment_tree", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_does_the_data_change", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_hierarchy_of_blocks", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model / Pitfalls", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_over_difference_array", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_tree", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Choosing: the decision table", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_tree", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_selection_and_order_statistics_learning_maintain_structure_not_statistic", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Use Cases \u2014 Fenwick over value-buckets as the dynamic rank structure, links ../selection-and-order-statistics/learning.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_sparse_table", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_segment_tree", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfall: Building a Fenwick tree for min or max", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_recursion_and_backtracking_learning_make_unmake_invariant", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_lazy_propagation", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Both maintain a paired down/up state obligation that any missed code path breaks silently and order-dependently", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "invertibility_determines_the_range_structure", "label": "Invertibility Determines Which Range Structure You Can Use", "nodes": ["data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_invertibility_requirement", "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_sum_array", "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_tree", "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_segment_tree", "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_sparse_table"], "relation": "participate_in", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/range-query-structures/learning.md"}]}